  "tip": "Time to put Unit 2 together. Check yourself on the pronoun grid (ordinary → polite):\n\n- **I / we:** আমি / আমরা\n- **you:** তুই, তুমি / তোরা, তোমরা → **আপনি / আপনারা**\n- **he, she / they:** সে, ও / তারা, ওরা → **তিনি, উনি / ওনারা**\n\nNew words: **বাংলা** is the *language* (Bengali); **বাংলাদেশি** is the *nationality*; **ইংরেজি** is English. Bengali speakers on both sides of the border call themselves **বাঙালি** (*bangali*) — an ethnic and linguistic identity, not a nationality.\n\nBangladesh is one of very few countries named after its language: *Bangla-desh* = 'Bangla country'.",
